ere has been a significant slowing over the past several quarters. Growth\n\nSeptember 2007\n\nPROFILE OF THE ECONOMY\n\n7\n\nduring the 12 months through June is still the second slowest since the second quarter of 1999.\n\nUnit labor costs, which represent the interaction of productivity and compensation, increased 2.1 percent at an annual rate in the second quarter, slowing from the first quarter's 3.0 percent rise. These costs were up 4.5 percent over the latest four quarters.","stderr":"","exit_code":0},"isError":false}}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
